  "worked_solution": "To find the roots of the polynomial, we must solve the equation $p(y)=0,$ that is\n\n$$\n8{y}^{4}+4{y}^{3}-12{y}^{2}=0.\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that all of the terms of the polynomial have a common factor of $4{y}^{2}.$ We can factor out the $4{y}^{2}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{y}^{2}(2{y}^{2}+y-3) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we factor the expression $2{y}^{2}+y-3$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{y}^{2}(2{y}^{2}+y-3) & =0 \\\\ 4{y}^{2}(2y+3)(y-1) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, by applying the zero product rule, the solutions are $y=0,$ $y=-\\frac{3}{2},$ and $y=1.$",
